+- The owner requested investigation and resolution of the three remaining browser-suite failures: one US-02 keyboard-focus case and two US-01 checks relying on manually modified Strapi vehicle-make options. The request required approved-requirement traceability, tests against both the existing development catalog and fresh seeds, independent QA and review, preservation of behavior and evidence, and no Git mutations. The approved [US-01](spec/US-01.md) and [US-02](spec/US-02.md) requirements and ADR-001 through ADR-004 were the reference; no spec or architecture change was needed.
+- The orchestrator used `debugging-and-error-recovery` and `test-driven-development`. It delegated E2E changes to `/root/browser_failures_developer` (Developer, configured `gpt-6.2-sol` / `low`), independent execution and reporting to `/root/browser_failures_qa` (QA, configured `gpt-6-luna` / `xhigh`), and a separate code review to `/root/browser_failures_review` (Reviewer, configured `gpt-6-luna` / `high`). Each agent received the scoped correction task, the applicable approved artifacts, the requirement to preserve history, and the prohibition on staging, committing or pushing. The Developer changed only `e2e/us01.spec.ts`, `e2e/us01-qa.spec.ts` and `e2e/us02-qa.spec.ts`; QA appended to [the existing US-02 report](reports/qa/US-02-qa-report.md); the Reviewer appended to [the existing US-02 review](reviews/US-02-review.md).
