+- The prior keyboard failure did not reproduce in the deterministic fresh-stack baseline, nor in 20 repeated keyboard-case executions. No application focus defect was observed. The former harness programmatically focused the radio and did not clearly sequence the user's natural Tab entry and Continue's enabled-state transition. The revised test starts from the focused heading, Tabs to the native radio, chooses Ruta with ArrowDown, checks disabled-to-enabled state, then Tabs through Back and Continue and activates the handoff with Enter. The resulting assertions follow AC-US02-04/07 and do not expect a disabled control to receive focus.
